  "caption": "Gifford et al. 2014 Lab Chip 14, 4496\u20134505, Fig. 6 (the micrograph; scale from the printed 125 \u00b5m centre, 4.5248 \u00b5m/px; the rows at 49.81\u00b0 on the image) with the mask gifford2014_fig6_aligned, all four legs on ONE map, fitted on the ends of legs 5, 3 and 1 (cyan: the claim, legs 5, 3 and 1 with their divider walls and their turns as far as the frame shows them, leg 7 to 4 rows before its drawn end; amber: the outlet stretch and leg 7's end).  Registration: scale and rotation from the printed centre width and the rows on the image, rotation measured on the image; translation fitted on features and, independently, by chamfer matching (they agree within 0.0 / 0.1 px along / across).  Nearest-outline offset: median 0.82 \u00b5m, 90th percentile 2.19 \u00b5m (n 21916); for comparison 1.74 \u00b5m with the mask shifted half a pitch along and 2.64 \u00b5m with it shifted 5 \u00b5m across.  Over every eligible sample: the metric found an outline for 96.5 % of the 22700 eligible samples (coverage 0.965); censored null ratios 7.93 (half a pitch) and 4.35 (5 \u00b5m across); chamfer null ratios 2.47 and 1.76.  The leg axes are the preset's (reproduction.leg_Y), read on this image without the mask (legs 1, 3, 5, 7 on the post rows; legs 2, 4, 6 from the turns' common centre, a semicircle assumed), so the turns' radii and their centre across the rows agree with the image by construction (consistency, not a test): the image's 16 walls lie a median 1.6 \u00b5m (90th percentile 4.0) from the mask's nearest edge, and about the image's turn centre the mask's walls lie at radii +0.8 \u00b1 1.8 \u00b5m from the image's (the side channels' own offset included).  The independent turn result is along the flow, which nothing read on the turns sets: fitted alone, the mask's turn centre lies 5.8 \u00b5m downstream of the image's (and 8.2 \u00b5m across).  Leg 7, not in the fit, lies 0.31 \u00b5m across from where its own end registers it; its drawn end is 103 \u00b5m (2 rows) beyond the image's (pc_last_short moves it in steps of about n - 1 rows: LIMITATIONS 25).",
